			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825496">
									

<p>Adding on to the above, the Axis powers weren't the only ones developing technology at a breakneck speed during WWII.</p>
<p>The British, for instance, were heavily dependent vulnerable tanker shipments from the Middle East and the US for oil throughout the war, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petroleum_Warfare_Department">The Petroleum Warfare Department</a> was created both to help ensure the British oil supply and utilize the fact that they oddly never did seem to run out in the end. Operation Pluto in particular is an awesomely named project that in the real world involved building an undersea pipeline from freshly liberated France to Britain in an absurdly short timeframe- but maybe that was just a cover for where they were actually making oil manifest from?</p>
<p>(May add more to this later)</p>

